# Environment Variables Documentation

## Required Variables

### Database
- `MONGO_URI` - MongoDB connection string
  - Format: `mongodb://...` or `mongodb+srv://...`
  - Example: `mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/dbname`

### Authentication
- `JWT_SECRET` - Secret key for JWT token signing
  - Should be at least 32 characters long
  - Example: `your-super-secret-jwt-key-min-32-chars`

### Server
- `PORT` - Port number for the server
  - Default: `5000`
  - Example: `5000`

## Optional Variables

### Environment
- `NODE_ENV` - Environment mode
  - Values: `development`, `production`, `test`
  - Default: `development`
- `ENABLE_CONSOLE_LOGS` - Force enable console logs in production (optional)
  - Values: `true`, `false`
  - Default: `false` (console.log is muted in production by default)

### CORS
- `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` - Comma-separated list of allowed origins
  - Example: `http://localhost:3000,https://yourdomain.com`
  - Default: `http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001`

### Cloudinary (File Uploads)
- `CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME` - Cloudinary cloud name
- `CLOUDINARY_API_KEY` - Cloudinary API key
- `CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET` - Cloudinary API secret

### Payment Gateways
- `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` - Razorpay key ID
- `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` - Razorpay key secret
- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` - Stripe secret key
- `PAYTM_MID` - Paytm Merchant ID
- `PAYTM_MERCHANT_KEY` - Paytm Merchant Key (for staging, this is usually 16 characters)
- `PAYTM_WEBSITE` - Paytm Website (e.g., WEBSTAGING)
- `PAYTM_INDUSTRY_TYPE_ID` - Paytm Industry Type
- `PAYTM_CALLBACK_URL` - Paytm Callback URL (e.g., http://localhost:5000/api/payments/paytm/callback)

### MSG91 (SMS/OTP Service)
- `MSG91_AUTH_KEY` - MSG91 authentication key (get from https://msg91.com/)
  - **IMPORTANT**: DLT template is MANDATORY for sending SMS in India
  - For development, comment this out to log OTPs to console instead
  - For production, you MUST have an approved DLT template
- `MSG91_SENDER_ID` - Sender ID for SMS (optional, defaults to "MSGIND")
- `MSG91_TEMPLATE_ID` - DLT Template ID for OTP SMS (required for India)

### WhatsApp Cloud API (Meta)
- `WHATSAPP_API_VERSION` - Graph API version (default: `v19.0`)
- `WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID` - Meta WhatsApp Business Phone Number ID
- `WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN` - Permanent System User Access Token with `whatsapp_business_messaging` permission
- `WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_NEW_APPLICATION` - Approved template for new worker application (default: `new_application`)
- `WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_WORKER_HIRED` - Approved template for hired notification (default: `worker_hired`)
- `WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_JOB_SUGGESTION` - Approved template for matched job suggestions (default: `job_suggestion`)
- `WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_WORKER_SUGGESTION` - Approved template for matched worker suggestions (default: `worker_suggestion`)
- `WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_ADMIN_ANNOUNCEMENT` - Approved template for admin broadcast announcements (default: `admin_announcement`)

## Example .env File

```env
# Required
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/shramik_seva
JWT_SECRET=your-super-secret-jwt-key-at-least-32-characters-long
PORT=5000

# Optional
NODE_ENV=development
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001

# Cloudinary
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your-cloud-name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your-api-key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your-api-secret

# Razorpay
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your-razorpay-key-id
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=your-razorpay-key-secret

# Stripe
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=your-stripe-secret-key

# MSG91
MSG91_AUTH_KEY=your-msg91-auth-key
MSG91_SENDER_ID=MSGIND
MSG91_TEMPLATE_ID=your-template-id

# WhatsApp Cloud API (Meta)
WHATSAPP_API_VERSION=v19.0
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=your-whatsapp-phone-number-id
WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=your-whatsapp-system-user-access-token
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_NEW_APPLICATION=new_application
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_WORKER_HIRED=worker_hired
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_JOB_SUGGESTION=job_suggestion
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_WORKER_SUGGESTION=worker_suggestion
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_ADMIN_ANNOUNCEMENT=admin_announcement
```

## Production Deployment

### Environment-Specific Settings

**Development:**
- Rate limiting is relaxed
- Detailed error messages
- Request logging enabled
- CORS allows all localhost origins

**Production:**
- Strict rate limiting
- Generic error messages (no stack traces)
- Only critical request logging
- CORS restricted to specified origins
- HTTPS enforcement via Helmet
- Security headers enabled

### Security Checklist

- [ ] Change `JWT_SECRET` to a strong random string (min 32 chars)
- [ ] Set `NODE_ENV=production`
- [ ] Configure `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` with your production domain(s)
- [ ] Use strong MongoDB credentials
- [ ] Enable MongoDB IP whitelist
- [ ] Use environment-specific API keys for payment gateways
- [ ] Never commit `.env` file to version control
- [ ] Use secrets management service in production (AWS Secrets Manager, etc.)

### Verifying Environment

The server will automatically validate environment variables on startup and:
- ✅ Show success message if all required variables are present
- ❌ Throw error and exit if required variables are missing
- ⚠️  Show warnings for missing optional variables in production
